WEBVTT

00:02.570 --> 00:12.380
♪♪

00:12.410 --> 00:13.680
♪♪

00:13.710 --> 00:16.810
HUE: The outcome was never
in our favor, Gary.

00:16.850 --> 00:18.650
Gary:
Cut it to me straight, HUE.

00:18.680 --> 00:20.750
What are my chances of
getting out of this mess?

00:20.780 --> 00:22.350
In your current state,

00:22.390 --> 00:25.820
you will pass the point
of recovery in 10 minutes.

00:25.850 --> 00:28.390
You are also leaking O2,
Gary.

00:30.090 --> 00:31.260
Huh, look at that.

00:31.290 --> 00:33.360
They went with green
for a red alert.

00:33.400 --> 00:35.500
I mean, I would have
went with red,

00:35.530 --> 00:36.830
a periwinkle.

00:36.870 --> 00:39.070
Heck, I mean, even egg nog.

00:39.100 --> 00:40.400
I don't even know
if that's a color,

00:40.440 --> 00:42.840
but, oh, good Lord,
now I just want egg nog.

00:42.870 --> 00:44.270
The rate of the leak

00:44.310 --> 00:46.740
will render you lifeless
in nine minutes.

00:46.780 --> 00:50.710
You are really buttering me
up with fantastic news.

00:50.750 --> 00:52.250
I'm afraid, Gary,

00:52.280 --> 00:54.920
there is no foreseeable
outcome where you survive.

00:54.950 --> 00:58.390
These tickets suck --
right in the nosebleeds.

00:58.420 --> 01:08.430
♪♪

01:08.460 --> 01:17.440
♪♪

01:17.470 --> 01:27.780
♪♪

01:27.820 --> 01:30.220
♪♪

01:30.250 --> 01:33.190
[ Lights powering on ]

01:35.860 --> 01:38.960
[ Beeping ]

01:40.530 --> 01:42.300
Aah!

01:42.330 --> 01:43.730
HUE:
Good morning, Gary.

01:43.770 --> 01:46.800
Day 1,818.

01:46.840 --> 01:48.570
How about freakin' no?

01:48.600 --> 01:49.970
[ Grunts ]

01:50.010 --> 01:52.610
That was a bit harder
than normal, HUE!

01:52.640 --> 02:02.950
♪♪

02:02.990 --> 02:05.590
[ Electricity crackling ]

02:05.620 --> 02:14.700
♪♪

02:14.730 --> 02:16.470
Hello, dear friend.

02:19.130 --> 02:20.770
It's been a while.

02:20.800 --> 02:21.970
[ Footsteps ]

02:22.000 --> 02:23.940
Hey! Yes!

02:23.970 --> 02:25.110
What's up, Hank?

02:25.140 --> 02:28.340
[ Electricity crackles ]

02:28.380 --> 02:29.550
Hmm, yeah.

02:29.580 --> 02:32.480
Beth is looking good today.
Look at that.

02:32.520 --> 02:35.520
Staring at me
with those hot eyes.

02:35.550 --> 02:39.020
You, me...later.

02:39.050 --> 02:40.320
Cards, Hank?
You want to play?

02:40.360 --> 02:41.790
I need somebody
to play with.

02:41.820 --> 02:45.230
So it's gonna be you.
Aah!

02:45.260 --> 02:49.030
I'm starting to run
out of decks, Hank.

02:49.060 --> 02:51.070
[ Laughing ]
Hey, Gary! Hello!

02:51.100 --> 02:54.540
Ooh, cookie, yummy!

02:54.570 --> 02:55.870
Ha!

02:55.900 --> 02:57.170
-HUE?
-Yes, Gary?

02:57.210 --> 02:58.240
Can I have a cookie?

02:58.270 --> 03:00.010
Mm, no, Gary.

03:00.040 --> 03:01.640
Why not?

03:01.680 --> 03:02.980
You opened it for KVN.

03:03.010 --> 03:05.550
That sack of wet turds
can't even eat cookies!

03:05.580 --> 03:08.720
He just smashes it
into his processor slot.

03:08.750 --> 03:10.250
I hate KVN...
so painfully.

03:10.290 --> 03:12.050
He's the blight
of my life.

03:12.090 --> 03:13.720
If you take a cookie,

03:13.760 --> 03:16.730
I will be forced to add
one full day to your sentence.

03:16.760 --> 03:18.530
[ Laughs ]

03:18.560 --> 03:21.000
[ Both laughing ]

03:21.030 --> 03:25.330
You think a full day
scares the captain?

03:25.370 --> 03:27.740
Gary, I've explained
this to you every day

03:27.770 --> 03:29.740
for the past five years.

03:29.770 --> 03:31.110
You are not the captain.

03:31.140 --> 03:32.780
You are a prisoner
aboard this ship.

03:32.810 --> 03:36.250
Sounds vaguely familiar.
Now, open this cabinet.

03:36.280 --> 03:39.050
Oh, they're just
so-o-o-o good!

03:39.080 --> 03:40.250
Mmm, mmm, mmm!

03:40.280 --> 03:41.750
[ Grunts ]
Aaaah!

03:41.780 --> 03:44.020
One day has been added
to your sentence.

03:44.050 --> 03:45.690
Oh! I touched one!

03:45.720 --> 03:48.120
The captain's touched one!

03:48.160 --> 03:50.860
Captain's log 80085.

03:50.890 --> 03:52.730
Hey, Quinn! Guess who!

03:52.760 --> 03:55.560
It's me, Gary, again.
Quinn, I've thought on it,

03:55.600 --> 03:57.570
and I've decided that
since this is a big day,

03:57.600 --> 03:59.770
the day of our anniversary,
as you know,

03:59.800 --> 04:02.100
it's time to get real.

04:02.140 --> 04:06.280
Quinn, this --
this is the real raw Gary.

04:06.310 --> 04:08.110
It's been eating me up inside

04:08.140 --> 04:09.910
keeping the real
raw Gary from you.

04:09.950 --> 04:11.380
For five years,

04:11.410 --> 04:13.320
real raw Gary hasn't been able

04:13.350 --> 04:15.280
to get you out
of his mind fortress.

04:15.320 --> 04:18.390
When I met you that day,
I knew you were it.

04:18.420 --> 04:20.790
Give us what's ours, Gary!

04:20.820 --> 04:23.160
Technically, it's mine!

04:23.190 --> 04:25.990
Dr. Bluesteen and Derek!
-Lose some weight!

04:26.030 --> 04:27.960
Come on, Derek, keep up!

04:28.000 --> 04:29.470
They gave me a seltzer?

04:29.500 --> 04:31.930
Why would they give me a
seltzer...unless I ordered it.

04:31.970 --> 04:34.200
Did I order it?
Yes, I did!

04:36.270 --> 04:37.770
I'm gonna break
your knees, Gary!

04:37.810 --> 04:39.810
[ Sighs ]

04:39.840 --> 04:44.150
[ Heavenly music plays ]

04:44.180 --> 04:45.750
Sweet heavenly fire.

04:45.780 --> 04:49.150
Who is the muy bueno
super spicy lady?

04:49.180 --> 04:51.490
Captain Quinn Aragon.
But don't bother.

04:51.520 --> 04:53.620
If you're not Infinity Guard,
she's not interested.

04:53.660 --> 04:57.830
Actually, I'm pretty freaking
high up in the command chain.

04:57.860 --> 04:58.860
-Really?
-Yeah, really.

04:58.890 --> 05:00.300
Seriously?

05:00.330 --> 05:02.630
Seriously, I can't get any
closer to your face, dude.

05:02.670 --> 05:04.600
Then where's
your uniform, bud?

05:04.630 --> 05:05.800
I have one, guy.

05:05.830 --> 05:09.510
-No, you don't, pal.
-Yes, I do, chum!

05:09.540 --> 05:13.010
It's...in the bathroom.
Crap!

05:13.040 --> 05:15.080
-[ Whistling ]
-Shwa!

05:16.880 --> 05:20.220
Looking good, Gary!

05:20.250 --> 05:22.350
You're just gonna
leave him in there,

05:22.390 --> 05:26.020
you chuck -- you chuck-face!

05:26.050 --> 05:28.890
Oh, sweet aspirin.

05:28.920 --> 05:31.030
Three dratnoids, exact change!

05:31.060 --> 05:32.060
Tight!

05:32.090 --> 05:33.830
[ Clinks, beeps ]

05:36.900 --> 05:38.700
Swallow!

05:38.730 --> 05:41.340
You're a good guy, Gary.

05:42.570 --> 05:45.870
Now to be smooth as --
Uh! Uh!

05:45.910 --> 05:47.040
Hmm-hmm-hmm.

05:47.080 --> 05:49.010
First time
I got a girl's number

05:49.040 --> 05:52.210
before
I even said "Hey."

05:52.250 --> 05:53.550
You see, I like that.

05:53.580 --> 05:55.650
I like a girl
with a lot of phones.

05:55.680 --> 05:58.390
Actually, this is the solution
to an internal inconsistency

05:58.420 --> 06:00.220
in Planck's constant
that's never been solved

06:00.260 --> 06:02.930
because until now, no one
realized it was a problem.

06:02.960 --> 06:05.330
And speaking of problems,
maybe you should leave

06:05.360 --> 06:07.600
before you become one --
as in now.

06:07.630 --> 06:09.100
Or I could
buy you a drink.

06:09.130 --> 06:11.000
-Really?
-Let's get wild.

06:11.030 --> 06:13.540
How about you
buy me a drink?

06:13.570 --> 06:17.170
Wow.
I mean, no. But wow.

06:17.210 --> 06:18.540
All Infinity Guards,

06:18.570 --> 06:20.440
report back to base
immediately.

06:20.480 --> 06:22.410
-Let's go!
-Back to your place?

06:22.450 --> 06:24.180
You're moving
at cheetah speeds.

06:24.210 --> 06:25.380
I like it.

06:25.410 --> 06:28.750
You have
an F71 Hawk to fly, pilot.

06:28.780 --> 06:31.420
Oh, my crap.

06:34.320 --> 06:36.060
Move this Hawk, pilot.

06:36.090 --> 06:37.590
You can do this, Gary.

06:37.630 --> 06:40.460
Become a much
smarter person now.

06:43.330 --> 06:45.070
Oh, my double crap!

06:45.100 --> 06:48.200
[ Explosion! ]

06:48.240 --> 06:49.940
You're not a pilot,
are you?

06:49.970 --> 06:53.140
-Yes, I am.
-Punch!

06:53.180 --> 06:54.480
[ Bang! Clink! ]

06:54.510 --> 06:56.280
Gary: Lesson learned.

06:56.310 --> 06:58.310
If you ever want to piss
off a whole government,

06:58.350 --> 06:59.950
just take out 92 star cruisers

06:59.980 --> 07:02.750
and a small family-owned
Mexican restaurant.

07:02.790 --> 07:04.950
Sorry, Guadalupe.

07:04.990 --> 07:06.960
Hyuh!

07:06.990 --> 07:09.460
-Wah!
-[ Laughing ]

07:09.490 --> 07:10.830
Hey, Gary.
My name is KVN.

07:10.860 --> 07:13.430
I'm your deep space insanity
avoidance companion.

07:13.460 --> 07:15.800
Nice to meet you.
-I already hate you.

07:15.830 --> 07:18.330
The good news is that
I only have a week left

07:18.370 --> 07:20.770
to my sentence aboard
this pathetic rat's nest.

07:20.800 --> 07:23.340
And send! She's gonna
respond this time, HUE.

07:23.370 --> 07:25.970
HUE: There is a high
probability she will not.

07:26.010 --> 07:28.680
But there's still a low
probability she will.

07:28.710 --> 07:29.650
I'll take it!

07:29.680 --> 07:31.880
Ha ha ha ha!
Nailed it!

07:33.580 --> 07:36.150
HUE: There are still arrays
that need to be repaired.

07:36.180 --> 07:39.520
Get off my cheeks, HUE.
-Get off my cheeks, Gary.

07:41.460 --> 07:44.230
Gary:
1891-C is back online.

07:47.700 --> 07:51.500
HUE...by any chance,
is it still Thursday?

07:51.530 --> 07:54.800
It's been Thursday
for the last 72 hours.

07:54.840 --> 07:57.340
Sweet.
Then it's still on.

08:00.640 --> 08:04.950
My name is Eduardo Montoya
Talakinto Ta Lacara Poligia.

08:04.980 --> 08:07.550
You killed my father.
Prepare to die.

08:07.580 --> 08:09.220
Gary,
your break is over.

08:09.250 --> 08:13.190
But the guy who killed Eduardo
Talakinto Tala Pacia's father

08:13.220 --> 08:15.560
hasn't prepared to die yet!

08:15.590 --> 08:18.690
Dang, there's a --
there's a pixel on the loose.

08:22.400 --> 08:24.630
-Whoo!
-Oh!

08:24.670 --> 08:26.330
It's an alien on my face!

08:26.370 --> 08:28.300
It's an alien on my --
it's a face alien!

08:28.340 --> 08:31.210
Aaaahh!

08:31.240 --> 08:35.680
Oh. You're not a face-eater,
you're a face-hugger.

08:35.710 --> 08:36.710
Chocli.

08:36.750 --> 08:38.680
I need a face-hugger
in my life.

08:38.710 --> 08:40.050
Whoa!

08:40.080 --> 08:43.320
You remind me of a friend
I used to have a long time ago.

08:43.350 --> 08:49.930
♪♪

08:49.960 --> 08:52.060
How do you like
the name Mooncake?

08:52.090 --> 08:53.330
Whoa!

08:53.360 --> 08:55.660
[ Chuckles ]
Mooncake it is.

08:55.700 --> 08:57.430
I'm pumped -- super-excited.

08:57.470 --> 08:59.200
You don't by chance
speak real words, do you?

08:59.230 --> 09:01.400
-Chocli-pop.
-Ha! Works for me.

09:05.770 --> 09:08.280
[ Grunts ]

09:08.310 --> 09:10.880
Welcome.

09:10.910 --> 09:12.850
[ Laughs evilly ]

09:12.880 --> 09:14.980
[ Laughing ]

09:17.790 --> 09:20.590
You're so tiny, man!
What -- oh!

09:20.620 --> 09:22.760
Wait until the guys
hear about this.

09:22.790 --> 09:25.130
Sit.

09:25.160 --> 09:26.260
[ Creaking ]

09:26.290 --> 09:27.800
[ Whimpering ]

09:31.130 --> 09:32.700
Where is it?!

09:32.740 --> 09:34.970
-What?!
-E-351.

09:35.000 --> 09:36.100
I -- I don't know.

09:36.140 --> 09:37.970
I would never lie to you,
Lord Commander.

09:38.010 --> 09:40.540
[ Laughs ]

09:40.580 --> 09:41.640
You know, it's just --

09:41.680 --> 09:43.280
I'm sorry,
you're just so small!

09:43.310 --> 09:44.610
It's -- it's...

09:44.650 --> 09:47.120
Wah!

09:47.150 --> 09:49.550
Where did you find it?

09:49.580 --> 09:52.790
I didn't.
It found me.

09:54.960 --> 09:55.960
The less HUE --

09:55.990 --> 09:58.460
who, between us,
is a bit of a dick --

09:58.490 --> 09:59.830
knows about you, the better.

09:59.860 --> 10:01.300
Okay, let's get you in here.

10:01.330 --> 10:03.670
You ready?
-Chocli!

10:03.700 --> 10:06.640
Chocli, chocli!
-Please close.

10:06.670 --> 10:09.140
Okay, it's not fitting.
It's not working.

10:09.170 --> 10:12.310
I hide there sometimes.
I'm like a mattress ghost.

10:12.340 --> 10:13.910
Don't tell anyone.
-Ooh.

10:13.940 --> 10:16.510
Oh, perfect!
Per-- no, it's not perfect.

10:16.540 --> 10:18.650
That sucks.
Why does that suck so hard?!

10:18.680 --> 10:20.250
Okay, how about this?

10:20.280 --> 10:22.950
Sometimes I hide --
I like to hide from myself

10:22.990 --> 10:25.790
by putting underwear on
the circumference of my head.

10:25.820 --> 10:27.320
How about that?
How's it fit?

10:27.360 --> 10:29.120
-Chocli.
-Perfect.

10:29.160 --> 10:31.830
[ Groaning ]

10:31.860 --> 10:36.400
Please...just...
kill...me!

10:39.170 --> 10:43.010
Wouldn't think of it.
That would be rude.

10:43.040 --> 10:44.270
Eat.

10:44.310 --> 10:46.140
[ Growls ]

10:46.170 --> 10:48.740
[ Crunching ]

10:51.180 --> 10:52.610
HUE, what is going on?

10:52.650 --> 10:54.650
Why has the ship turned
into a silent dance rave?

10:54.680 --> 10:56.120
HUE:
Four unknown vessels

10:56.150 --> 10:58.120
are descending
upon our location.

10:58.150 --> 10:59.720
The markings lead me
to believe

10:59.760 --> 11:01.520
they are Ventrexian
bounty hunters.

11:01.560 --> 11:04.860
Twist my nipples rough, we're
talking complex life-forms.

11:04.890 --> 11:07.630
Yes! HUE, you must find out
if they play cards.

11:07.660 --> 11:09.660
I need this!
I need this, HUE!

11:09.700 --> 11:12.200
I -- I really need
somebody to play with.

11:12.230 --> 11:20.710
♪♪

11:20.740 --> 11:24.050
Activating
security protocol.

11:24.080 --> 11:25.580
HUE, what the crap?!

11:25.610 --> 11:27.020
For your own safety,

11:27.050 --> 11:28.550
you must remain
in the commissary.

11:28.580 --> 11:29.990
For my own safety?

11:30.020 --> 11:31.890
We get our first
visitors in five years,

11:31.920 --> 11:33.260
and I can't mingle with them?

11:33.290 --> 11:36.520
HUE, open this door right now!
I need to mingle!

11:36.560 --> 11:38.030
I'm afraid I cannot.

11:38.060 --> 11:40.030
You better afraid me
up an open door!

11:40.060 --> 11:42.160
-Ooh, let KVN help!
-God almighty, KVN!

11:42.200 --> 11:44.370
You can't just phantom
up on me like that!

11:44.400 --> 11:46.670
Don't worry about me,
I am helping.

11:46.700 --> 11:49.400
Oh, oh. KVN, you did
something right!

11:49.440 --> 11:50.740
Ohh!

11:50.770 --> 11:53.940
KVN, you processed
horrendous mess of wires!

11:53.980 --> 11:57.550
Lord Commander: Your vessel
has been subjected

11:57.580 --> 12:00.120
to a search
for specimen E-351.

12:00.150 --> 12:03.250
Come forward...or die.

12:03.290 --> 12:04.350
Oh, crap.

12:04.390 --> 12:11.460
♪♪

12:11.490 --> 12:14.460
My arm, man!
Aaahh!

12:14.500 --> 12:16.530
You fool!

12:16.560 --> 12:17.930
Who the freak is this guy?

12:17.970 --> 12:19.630
I believe they want
the alien

12:19.670 --> 12:21.270
you're hiding
in your backpack.

12:21.300 --> 12:24.140
What? I don't know
what you're referring to.

12:27.340 --> 12:31.610
This is what I was meant to do!
I have never felt so alive!

12:31.650 --> 12:33.980
Oh! You mean
my underpants caddy.

12:34.020 --> 12:38.550
Yes. We should comply
with their wishes, Gary.

12:38.590 --> 12:39.920
I don't know.

12:39.960 --> 12:41.720
I kind of was starting
to like this little guy.

12:41.760 --> 12:43.230
He gives great hugs.

12:43.260 --> 12:46.830
Gary, we are not equipped
to face this threat.

12:51.370 --> 12:54.800
-Good job, Avocato.
-This is not our fight.

12:54.840 --> 12:57.510
HUE, we make it our fight.
You're Infinity Guard.

12:57.540 --> 12:59.310
Your whole motto
is to protect life.

12:59.340 --> 13:01.110
Is that life, Gary?

13:01.140 --> 13:03.750
Well, if it isn't, then I'm
a raging sack of walnuts!

13:03.780 --> 13:07.150
HUE, lightfold the ship!

13:07.180 --> 13:08.980
This will lengthen
your sentence.

13:09.020 --> 13:11.020
I get it.
Lightfold the ship, HUE!

13:11.050 --> 13:12.650
Gary.

13:12.690 --> 13:14.120
Do it!

13:17.730 --> 13:20.330
They're lightfolding!

13:23.730 --> 13:26.470
[ All yelling ]

13:26.500 --> 13:29.170
[ Alarm blaring ]

13:29.200 --> 13:37.880
♪♪

13:37.910 --> 13:41.050
Proximity alert.
Proximity alert.

13:41.080 --> 13:42.380
Is that what I think it is?

13:42.420 --> 13:45.190
HUE, that's no good.
Get us out of here.

13:45.220 --> 13:47.190
Lightfold again,
lightfold, lightfold!

13:47.220 --> 13:48.320
We are immobilized

13:48.360 --> 13:50.160
until the lightfold
engines cool.

13:50.190 --> 13:54.200
The asteroids will reach
the ship in 29 seconds.

13:54.230 --> 13:55.830
Secure your helmet
immediately.

13:55.860 --> 13:56.970
My helmet's in the airlock.

13:57.000 --> 14:00.240
Run.
15 seconds until impact.

14:00.270 --> 14:02.840
At your current pace,
you will not make it.

14:02.870 --> 14:05.570
Oh, Gary will make it.

14:05.610 --> 14:06.880
Hey, Gary,
sorry, got a minute?

14:06.910 --> 14:09.210
Yeah, I've been
thinking about...

14:09.240 --> 14:11.380
[ Groans ]

14:11.410 --> 14:14.050
Hyah!

14:16.580 --> 14:18.220
Gary, two seconds.

14:18.250 --> 14:20.790
You're gonna live!
You're gonna live!

14:24.460 --> 14:28.060
Sweet Grandor's glove!
Definitely gonna die this time!

14:32.100 --> 14:34.500
HUE: Gary, you may
have a problem.

14:34.540 --> 14:36.070
I seriously question
your usage of "may have."

14:36.100 --> 14:39.670
I think we have reached have.
I am very deep in have!

14:39.710 --> 14:41.180
Due to
the moon's gravity,

14:41.210 --> 14:44.610
the asteroid field will swing
back to the Galaxy 1

14:44.650 --> 14:48.350
and then at you in
approximately 39 seconds.

14:48.380 --> 14:49.680
That's no good, HUE.

14:49.720 --> 14:51.250
Formulate me up
some solutions.

14:51.290 --> 14:53.020
Calculating. Mm-hmm.

14:53.060 --> 14:54.360
Mmm.

14:54.390 --> 14:56.560
Mnh-mnh.

14:56.590 --> 14:57.690
Ahh.

14:57.730 --> 14:59.730
Gary, I do have a solution

14:59.760 --> 15:02.400
with a 33% chance
of success.

15:02.430 --> 15:03.930
Okay, and that would be?

15:03.970 --> 15:06.940
Perform an emergency air
blow-out of your O2 tanks.

15:06.970 --> 15:08.770
If you can enter
the moon's orbit,

15:08.800 --> 15:11.240
you might be able to
sling-hook around it

15:11.270 --> 15:12.540
back to the Galaxy 1.

15:12.570 --> 15:14.940
All right. All right,
let's do this.

15:14.980 --> 15:16.880
Gary, you should know,

15:16.910 --> 15:19.710
this calculation
will only work with you.

15:19.750 --> 15:22.220
You will have to leave
the life-form behind.

15:22.250 --> 15:23.390
Mooncake?

15:23.420 --> 15:25.620
Or there is
zero probability

15:25.650 --> 15:28.820
you will make it back
to the Galaxy 1 alive.

15:28.860 --> 15:31.430
I get it.
I'll scream at you.

15:31.460 --> 15:32.830
Mooncake is coming with.

15:32.860 --> 15:34.900
You will never
make it, Gary.

15:34.930 --> 15:38.130
Your only chance is to perform
this maneuver alone.

15:38.170 --> 15:42.570
HUE, your lack of confidence
is positively depressing!

15:42.600 --> 15:44.410
Blowing the air tank
in three...

15:44.440 --> 15:45.570
Gary, please.

15:45.610 --> 15:47.340
-Two...
-You will fail.

15:47.380 --> 15:48.440
You're right.

15:48.480 --> 15:51.450
I will fail...upwards.

15:51.480 --> 15:57.750
♪♪

15:57.790 --> 16:00.460
Entering
into moon's orbit.

16:04.490 --> 16:07.100
Oh, no!
It's not working.

16:07.130 --> 16:08.830
At your current
rate of velocity,

16:08.860 --> 16:12.170
you will not make it
back to the Galaxy 1.

16:12.200 --> 16:18.340
♪♪

16:18.370 --> 16:20.280
You have failed, Gary.

16:20.310 --> 16:27.020
♪♪

16:27.050 --> 16:31.390
The asteroids will make
impact in five seconds.

16:34.090 --> 16:38.030
Four...

16:38.060 --> 16:40.330
Three...

16:40.360 --> 16:42.130
[ Beeping, steady beep ]

16:42.160 --> 16:46.230
Two...

16:46.270 --> 16:48.840
One.

16:48.870 --> 16:56.310
♪♪

16:56.340 --> 16:58.850
[ Chitters ]

16:58.880 --> 17:00.010
It worked!

17:00.050 --> 17:01.320
[ Laughing ]

17:01.350 --> 17:03.020
HUE!
And you said I could die!

17:03.050 --> 17:04.220
Ha!

17:04.250 --> 17:07.320
You were dead --
for five minutes.

17:07.360 --> 17:08.690
Are you for serious?

17:08.720 --> 17:11.160
I believe the life-form
saved your life.

17:11.190 --> 17:13.530
-Mooncake?
-Chocli, chocli.

17:13.560 --> 17:15.360
Thank you for saving my life.

17:15.400 --> 17:16.860
Wow.

17:16.900 --> 17:19.830
I am detecting one unknown
life-form still aboard.

17:19.870 --> 17:21.870
He is armed.
-What deck?

17:21.900 --> 17:25.340
4A. Sames
are already on route.

17:25.370 --> 17:30.510
♪♪

17:30.550 --> 17:33.780
Hand over E-351.

17:33.820 --> 17:38.590
Listen, buddy, I only have
one thing to say to you.

17:38.620 --> 17:41.660
Do you play cards?

17:43.730 --> 17:46.130
I'm gonna take that
as a yes!

17:46.160 --> 17:48.300
-Freeze!
-Oh, good Lord!

17:48.330 --> 17:49.730
Oh, my gosh.

17:49.760 --> 17:51.370
Just don't walk up on
somebody like that, Hank!

17:51.400 --> 17:53.370
I'm gonna crap my pants.
I thought you were a baby ghost

17:53.400 --> 17:54.870
or a ghost baby or something

17:54.900 --> 17:57.140
in between the ghost
baby spectrum.

17:57.170 --> 17:58.310
-Freeze!
-Aagh!

17:58.340 --> 18:00.440
Gary:
Freakin' crap, Hank!

18:01.840 --> 18:04.310
Isn't this great?
I mean, just us guys

18:04.350 --> 18:07.920
sitting here,
chillin', playin' cards.

18:07.950 --> 18:09.750
[ Mumbling ]

18:09.780 --> 18:12.090
You really know how to
sling the zingers, cat guy.

18:12.120 --> 18:13.460
The name's Avocato.

18:13.490 --> 18:15.760
No.
The name is loser!

18:15.790 --> 18:18.730
Eat it!
Four of a kind!

18:18.760 --> 18:19.990
You're oblivious
to this thing, aren't you?

18:20.030 --> 18:21.260
-What?
-That.

18:21.300 --> 18:22.430
-This?
-Yes! That.

18:22.460 --> 18:24.100
-Mooncake?
-What's a Mooncake?

18:24.130 --> 18:25.730
-This!
-That?

18:25.770 --> 18:27.470
Yes, that.
Please tell me
you didn't name E-351.

18:27.500 --> 18:29.500
-What's an E-3559?
-That.

18:29.540 --> 18:31.840
-This?
-Yes, freakin' that!

18:31.870 --> 18:32.940
I suppose I did.

18:32.970 --> 18:34.610
You don't know
what that is, do you?

18:34.640 --> 18:38.150
That is a planet-killer.

18:38.180 --> 18:41.120
[ Laughing ]

18:41.150 --> 18:42.620
Are you hearing this?

18:42.650 --> 18:44.590
Freakin' guy thinks Mooncake
is a planet-killer!

18:44.620 --> 18:47.020
What a freakin' --
oh, man!

18:47.050 --> 18:49.260
[ Laughing ]

18:49.290 --> 18:51.130
Shut your face hole,
KVN! Crap.

18:51.160 --> 18:52.460
So you think
this is funny?

18:52.490 --> 18:54.000
I'm serious.
-Are you?

18:54.030 --> 18:55.200
Yes. The Lord Commander

18:55.230 --> 18:56.860
is searching
the galaxy for it.

18:56.900 --> 19:00.300
You can't hide.
Wherever you go, he'll find you.

19:00.340 --> 19:03.470
Why should I believe you,
Mr. Whiskers?

19:03.510 --> 19:05.810
Call me that again,
and I'll kill you.

19:05.840 --> 19:08.510
Mm-hmm. I've insulted you.
You see, the truth is,

19:08.540 --> 19:10.510
I've never socialized
with a cat man before.

19:10.550 --> 19:12.650
My neighbor had a cat.
Loved to lick himself.

19:12.680 --> 19:14.020
You're not gonna do that,
right?

19:14.050 --> 19:16.520
Otherwise, we're gonna
have problems, friend.

19:16.550 --> 19:19.490
I'm not a cat,
I'm a Ventrexian.

19:19.520 --> 19:22.320
Got it. See, I'm
a Presbyterian myself.

19:22.360 --> 19:23.560
But I love all people.

19:23.590 --> 19:25.830
Just how I was raised.
-We're in danger.

19:25.860 --> 19:28.560
Listen, all of us
are in danger!

19:28.600 --> 19:31.530
Mooncake, look into
Gary's gelatinous marbles.

19:31.570 --> 19:33.800
As long as I draw breath
and you provide me

19:33.840 --> 19:35.800
with copious amounts
of adventure,

19:35.840 --> 19:38.670
I will be there for you.
We're a team now.

19:38.710 --> 19:40.540
And I'll let you
be my sidekick and such

19:40.580 --> 19:41.980
with a super
side order of what-not.

19:42.010 --> 19:43.310
HUE: Well said.

19:43.350 --> 19:44.550
[ Dings ]

19:44.580 --> 19:47.650
A cookie -- for me?!

19:47.680 --> 19:49.580
Yes, Gary. Take one.

19:49.620 --> 19:51.020
You displayed a quality

19:51.050 --> 19:52.820
I hadn't seen in you
previously --

19:52.850 --> 19:55.690
courage. Exemplary.
You earned it.

19:55.720 --> 19:58.030
And because
I am the captain.

19:58.060 --> 20:00.190
Cookie withdrawn.

20:00.230 --> 20:01.360
Aah!

20:01.400 --> 20:04.030
The penitent man
shall pass.

20:04.070 --> 20:06.270
Ohh!
I got one!

20:06.300 --> 20:08.370
Sweet Grandor's glove,

20:08.400 --> 20:11.340
I got
a mother-loving cookie!

20:11.370 --> 20:13.110
Gary:
This is a cookie, Quinn.

20:13.140 --> 20:15.780
HUE said I earned it
because I did things, Quinn.

20:15.810 --> 20:19.680
Dangerous things.
Cookie-earning things.

20:19.710 --> 20:23.590
Now to eat the fruits
of my greatness.

20:23.620 --> 20:27.690
-Mine!
-What? No!

20:27.720 --> 20:30.560
KVN! Oh, KVN!

20:34.160 --> 20:37.100
Gary? Gary? Gary?!

20:37.130 --> 20:40.070
Gary? Gary. Gary!

20:40.100 --> 20:41.400
Gary, are you sleeping?

20:41.440 --> 20:42.970
Wah-pa!

20:43.000 --> 20:45.470
Oh, okay. We're good.
Don't mind me.

20:45.510 --> 20:47.480
I'm -- I'm just
floating this way.

20:47.510 --> 20:49.040
This is the way
I like to go.

20:49.080 --> 20:52.610
Bye! This was my plan.
That's my path.

20:52.650 --> 20:53.920
[ Laughs ]

20:53.950 --> 21:04.730
♪♪

21:04.760 --> 21:07.930
Lord Commander:
All the pieces are in place.

21:10.300 --> 21:12.270
Let's play a little.
